  <prompt>
    Author the participant-junction **schema ADR** — the binding record for the `sprk_communicationparticipant` design (task 003) and the ADR-034 path-C comply-with-intent tension the spec surfaces (spec §ADR Tensions, owner-approved 2026-07-18). This ADR DOCUMENTS a locked design; it does not re-open it. Write BOTH forms — concise in `.claude/adr/` (MUST/MUST NOT, ~120–160 lines) and full history in `docs/adr/` (rationale + alternatives + consequences) — and flip both ADR INDEX rows to Accepted.

    **ADR number**: ADR-047 is RESERVED for `spaarke-notification-spine-r1` (do NOT claim it). Re-verify the next free slot at execution (expected **ADR-048**) via `ls .claude/adr/ADR-04*` + `.claude/adr/INDEX.md`; claim the lowest unreserved number.

    Codify, at minimum (spec FR-08 + §ADR Tensions + §New-Components lock the content):

    1. **Message-grain participant index.** `sprk_communicationparticipant` is a junction at **message grain** — parent lookup to `sprk_communication` only (Q-A); thread-level participation is DERIVED by rollup, never written as thread-grain rows. It makes participants queryable (powers `participant=`, FR-02) where the legacy `sprk_from/to/cc` `;`-joined TEXT cannot.
    2. **Two typed nullable person lookups (ADR-034 path-C comply-with-intent).** Identity is `sprk_systemuser` (→systemuser) + `sprk_contact` (→contact), **exactly one set** for a resolved person, **both null** for an unresolved external address. This is the load-bearing decision: document WHY two typed lookups honor ADR-034's *intent* (the tuple exists to avoid an awkward **6-target** polymorphic lookup + to forbid fuzzy text-name matching) — here there are only **2** person targets, so typed lookups give typed identity + no text-name matching PLUS FK integrity + DataGrid person-chip auto-derivation the Guid+type tuple can't. Path C (comply-with-intent), NOT a path-B amendment of ADR-034.
    3. **Unresolved external rows are first-class (Q-D).** `sprk_addresstext` (raw email) + `sprk_isresolved=false` (both person lookups null) so external parties stay filterable + back-fillable when a `contact` is later created; `participant=` never silently omits them.
    4. **Role precision.** `sprk_role` Choice {From, To, Cc, Bcc} gives per-role precision the text fields lack.
    5. **Populated by reuse, not a new mechanism.** Rows are written at capture/send (task 050) reusing `ParticipantCorrelationRung.QueryContactByEmailAsync` — no new resolution mechanism, no new AI dependency, no new external SDK.

    Write the concise form at `.claude/adr/ADR-0NN-communication-participant-index.md` and the full form at `docs/adr/ADR-0NN-communication-participant-index.md` (NN = the claimed slot). Update `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` (add the row, Accepted) + `docs/adr/INDEX.md`; add the required `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry; confirm reachability via the ADR INDEX row (root `CLAUDE.md` §17 already points at the INDEX). Mirror how ADR-046 was authored (messaging-r1 task 007). **MAIN-SESSION ONLY (§3 write boundary).**
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke platform architect. Authoritative on the Communication data model (ADR-045/ADR-046) and the ADR-034 membership/identity precedent. Fluent in the project's concise ADR conventions (`.claude/adr/`, MUST/MUST NOT, ~120–160 lines) and the full-history form (`docs/adr/`). You author a binding schema ADR whose central job is to argue the ADR-034 path-C comply-with-intent decision precisely, so `adr-check` and future readers see the tension resolved on the record.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The participant-junction ADR exists in both concise (`.claude/adr/`) and full (`docs/adr/`) forms, codifying the five-part decision with MUST/MUST NOT rules and a precise ADR-034 path-C comply-with-intent argument; both ADR INDEXes show it Accepted; reachable via the ADR INDEX row (root `CLAUDE.md` §17); `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` has the entry; passes `/adr-check` against `spec.md` with no contradiction against ADR-034/ADR-046/ADR-024. `ADR-047` is NOT claimed (reserved for notification-spine). Task 050 (participant-index write) builds against a landed governance anchor.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Spec FR-08 requires the schema ADR as an acceptance item ("schema ADR authored (§11 + the ADR-034 path-C tension)"). The junction (task 003) is a NEW entity whose identity modeling deliberately deviates from ADR-034's `(personId, personIdType)` tuple — that deviation is owner-approved via the CLAUDE.md §6.5 path-C (comply-with-intent) mechanism and MUST be documented at the point of decision (§6.5 forbids deferring the exception). This ADR is that documentation: it records why 2 typed lookups honor ADR-034's intent for a 2-target identity, so the deviation is on the record and `adr-check` validates against a landed anchor rather than flagging an undocumented divergence.

      §11 Component Justification (a NEW ADR): (1) **Existing overlap** — ADR-034 covers person↔record membership via the tuple, and ADR-045/046 cover the communication/thread model, but NONE documents a message-grain queryable participant index or the 2-typed-lookup identity choice; the decision is net-new. (2) **Extension instead** — this ADR EXTENDS the ADR-034 identity precedent (comply-with-intent) rather than amending it (path B) or forking a parallel identity mechanism; it cites ADR-034 as the intent it honors. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without the ADR, the junction's deviation from ADR-034 is an undocumented silent violation (§6.5 forbidden), `adr-check` on task 050 has no anchor to validate the participant write against, and future work could re-litigate the tuple-vs-typed-lookup choice or reintroduce text-name matching. Named governance failure, not "future flexibility."

      The ADR must correctly cite its neighbors: **ADR-034** (the identity intent it complies with — the central citation), **ADR-024** (regarding family — the junction is orthogonal, message-grain, not a regarding mechanism), **ADR-045/ADR-046** (the communication/thread model it indexes), **ADR-032** (Null-Object kill-switch / `Lazy<>` — if the participant-write path is feature-gated in 050, it uses symmetric registration), **ADR-038** (seam tests are the DoD for the write/query — task 080), **ADR-027** (the junction lives in the project managed solution). It documents the message-grain (Q-A), two-typed-lookup (Q-C), and unresolved-row (Q-D) owner decisions.
    </background>
