    Mirror messaging-r1 task 007 (ADR-046) exactly in workflow + structure — this is the participant-index sibling for the same subsystem. The central job of this ADR is the ADR-034 path-C argument: be precise that ADR-034's tuple exists to avoid a 6-target polymorphic lookup + forbid text-name matching, and that a 2-target identity honors that intent with typed lookups. This is comply-with-intent (path C), not an amendment.

    This ADR DOCUMENTS a locked design (spec FR-08, owner-approved 2026-07-18) — it does not re-open the field set or the grain. Blocks 050 (the participant-index write cites this ADR). Land it early in W0 so 050's `adr-check` has the anchor.

